@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il04-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il34-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-s344-s347-income`

-- TESTS for ss 344 to 347 (row IL-34). Expected values worked by hand from the Hebrew; the arithmetic is beside each group. Money is illustrative round
-- figures except where it says it is the Law's or the Institute's own (the basic amount 10,382, the Schedule K figures 51,910 and 3,442, the threshold 7,703).

§ `Tests: sections 344 to 347`

§§ `Fixtures`

-- 100 members. Services: housing 7.5% of the basic amount a month a member, and 2,100,000 of other benefits; depreciation 400,000 (90% counted); provident fund 2,400
-- and income tax 6,000 a member.
`the figures of a kibbutz of 100 members` MEANS `The figures for the monthly income of a member of a cooperative kibbutz` WITH
    `the cost to the kibbutz of supplying living and other benefits to its members` IS 2_100_000,
    `the number of members of the kibbutz at the end of the year` IS 100,
    `the depreciation expenses on its assets that do not produce income` IS 400_000,
    `what an employer would deduct for a provident fund from the member's work income` IS 2_400,
    `what an employer would deduct as income tax from the member's work income` IS 6_000
`the figures of a kibbutz with no members` MEANS `The figures for the monthly income of a member of a cooperative kibbutz` WITH
    `the cost to the kibbutz of supplying living and other benefits to its members` IS 2_100_000,
    `the number of members of the kibbutz at the end of the year` IS 0,
    `the depreciation expenses on its assets that do not produce income` IS 400_000,
    `what an employer would deduct for a provident fund from the member's work income` IS 2_400,
    `what an employer would deduct as income tax from the member's work income` IS 6_000

`profits with a surplus of 300,000` MEANS `The profits of a renewed kibbutz in a tax year` WITH
    `its taxable income under section 60A(a) of the Income Tax Ordinance` IS 1_000_000,
    `the incomes of its members on which contributions were paid` IS 600_000,
    `the incomes exempt from contributions under this Law` IS 100_000,
    `the part of the surplus actually paid to the members` IS 120_000,
    `the number of members of the renewed kibbutz` IS 60
`profits with a negative surplus` MEANS `The profits of a renewed kibbutz in a tax year` WITH
    `its taxable income under section 60A(a) of the Income Tax Ordinance` IS 500_000,
    `the incomes of its members on which contributions were paid` IS 600_000,
    `the incomes exempt from contributions under this Law` IS 100_000,
    `the part of the surplus actually paid to the members` IS 0,
    `the number of members of the renewed kibbutz` IS 60
`profits of a kibbutz with no members` MEANS `The profits of a renewed kibbutz in a tax year` WITH
    `its taxable income under section 60A(a) of the Income Tax Ordinance` IS 1_000_000,
    `the incomes of its members on which contributions were paid` IS 600_000,
    `the incomes exempt from contributions under this Law` IS 100_000,
    `the part of the surplus actually paid to the members` IS 0,
    `the number of members of the renewed kibbutz` IS 0

§§ `Section 344(a): the month of the income`

-- The payment date 15.3.2026: the income is February's; 15.1.2026: December 2025's.
#ASSERT `s 344(a) — the first day of the month whose income is the monthly income, for the payment date` (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1
#ASSERT `s 344(a) — the first day of the month whose income is the monthly income, for the payment date` (YMD 2026 1 15) EQUALS YMD 2025 12 1
#ASSERT `s 344(a) — the first day of the month whose income is the monthly income, for the payment date` (YMD 2026 12 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 11 1

§§ `Section 344(a)(1): a member of a cooperative kibbutz`

-- Basic amount 10,000 (illustrative). At "year": (7.5% x 10,000 x 12 = 9,000) + 2,100,000/100 = 21,000 + 90% x 400,000/100 = 3,600 + 2,400 + 6,000 = 42,000, a twelfth: 3,500.
#ASSERT `s 344(a)(1) — the monthly income of a member of a cooperative kibbutz, the basic amount under paragraph (3) being` 10_000 `, reading the period of the figures as` `the figures are for the year and the monthly income is a twelfth of their sum` `, the figures` `the figures of a kibbutz of 100 members` EQUALS 3_500
-- At "month": 750 + 21,000 + 3,600 + 2,400 + 6,000 = 33,750.
#ASSERT `s 344(a)(1) — the monthly income of a member of a cooperative kibbutz, the basic amount under paragraph (3) being` 10_000 `, reading the period of the figures as` `the figures are for the month asked about` `, the figures` `the figures of a kibbutz of 100 members` EQUALS 33_750
-- Declined at the switch: the two readings differ by a factor.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 344(a)(1) — the monthly income of a member of a cooperative kibbutz, the basic amount under paragraph (3) being` 10_000 `, the figures` `the figures of a kibbutz of 100 members` BECAUSE "section 344(a)(1) calls the combination the monthly income and does not say whether its figures are the year's or the month's"
#ASSERT `s 344(a)(1) — the reading this row takes of the period of the figures` EQUALS `the period of the figures is declined`
-- The Law's own 2026 basic amount under paragraph (3), 10,382: housing 778.65 a month a member; at "year" (778.65 x 12 = 9,343.8) + 21,000 + 3,600 + 2,400 + 6,000 = 42,343.8, a twelfth 3,528.65; at "month" 778.65 + 33,000 = 33,778.65.
#ASSERT `s 344(a)(1) — the monthly income of a member of a cooperative kibbutz, the basic amount under paragraph (3) being` 10_382 `, reading the period of the figures as` `the figures are for the year and the monthly income is a twelfth of their sum` `, the figures` `the figures of a kibbutz of 100 members` EQUALS 3_528.65
#ASSERT `s 344(a)(1) — the monthly income of a member of a cooperative kibbutz, the basic amount under paragraph (3) being` 10_382 `, reading the period of the figures as` `the figures are for the month asked about` `, the figures` `the figures of a kibbutz of 100 members` EQUALS 33_778.65
-- No members at the year's end.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 344(a)(1) — the monthly income of a member of a cooperative kibbutz, the basic amount under paragraph (3) being` 10_000 `, reading the period of the figures as` `the figures are for the month asked about` `, the figures` `the figures of a kibbutz with no members` BECAUSE "a cooperative kibbutz with no members at the end of the year has no monthly income per member"
-- (2): the income of the person whose place he fills.
#ASSERT `s 344(a)(2) — the income of a family member who fills the place of another, who is regarded as having` 12_345 EQUALS 12_345

§§ `Section 344(b) and (d)`

#ASSERT     `s 344(b) — the order adding classes of payments is validly made` (`An order extending the income of an employee, under section 344(b)` WITH `made by the Minister` IS TRUE, `after consulting the Minister of Finance` IS TRUE, `approved by the Labour and Welfare Committee` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 344(b) — the order adding classes of payments is validly made` (`An order extending the income of an employee, under section 344(b)` WITH `made by the Minister` IS TRUE, `after consulting the Minister of Finance` IS FALSE, `approved by the Labour and Welfare Committee` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 344(b) — the order adding classes of payments is validly made` (`An order extending the income of an employee, under section 344(b)` WITH `made by the Minister` IS TRUE, `after consulting the Minister of Finance` IS TRUE, `approved by the Labour and Welfare Committee` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 344(b) — the order adding classes of payments is validly made` (`An order extending the income of an employee, under section 344(b)` WITH `made by the Minister` IS FALSE, `after consulting the Minister of Finance` IS TRUE, `approved by the Labour and Welfare Committee` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT     `s 344(d) — a provision on a cooperative-kibbutz member's income is validly made: by the Minister` TRUE `, approved by the Finance Committee` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 344(d) — a provision on a cooperative-kibbutz member's income is validly made: by the Minister` TRUE `, approved by the Finance Committee` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 344(d) — a provision on a cooperative-kibbutz member's income is validly made: by the Minister` FALSE `, approved by the Finance Committee` TRUE

§§ `Section 344A: a member of a renewed kibbutz`

#ASSERT `s 344A(a) — the monthly income of a member to whom section 3A(a) applies: grossed-up member budget` 18_000 EQUALS 18_000
-- Surplus: 1,000,000 - 600,000 - 100,000 = 300,000.
#ASSERT `s 344A(h) — the renewed kibbutz's surplus, the profits` `profits with a surplus of 300,000` EQUALS 300_000
-- A negative surplus: 500,000 - 600,000 - 100,000 = -200,000: declined at the switch; nil; as it is.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 344A(h) — the renewed kibbutz's surplus, the profits` `profits with a negative surplus` BECAUSE "section 344A(h) defines the surplus as the taxable income less two sums and does not say what a negative result is"
#ASSERT `s 344A(h) — the renewed kibbutz's surplus, reading a negative one as` `a negative surplus is nil` `, the profits` `profits with a negative surplus` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 344A(h) — the renewed kibbutz's surplus, reading a negative one as` `a negative surplus is taken as it is` `, the profits` `profits with a negative surplus` EQUALS -200_000
#ASSERT `s 344A(h) — the reading this row takes of a negative surplus` EQUALS `a negative surplus is declined`
-- (f): (300,000 - 120,000) / 60 = 3,000 a member.
#ASSERT `s 344A(f) — the annual income attributed to each member from the surplus not paid, the profits` `profits with a surplus of 300,000` EQUALS 3_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 344A(f) — the annual income attributed to each member from the surplus not paid, the profits` `profits with a negative surplus` BECAUSE "section 344A(h) defines the surplus as the taxable income less two sums and does not say what a negative result is"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 344A(f) — the annual income attributed to each member from the surplus not paid, the profits` `profits of a kibbutz with no members` BECAUSE "a renewed kibbutz with no members has no surplus to divide"

§§ `Section 345: the annual income of another insured person`

-- 200,000 - 15,000 - 5,000 = 180,000; with the small-business deduction of s 87B in play the s 47A deduction is not taken: 200,000 - 5,000 = 195,000.
#ASSERT `s 345(b)(1) — the annual income of another insured person` (`An insured person's assessed income for section 345` WITH `the income in the final assessment, before any exemption, deduction or credit` IS 200_000, `the contributions and equivalent tax allowed as a deduction under section 47A` IS 15_000, `the small-business deduction of section 87B applies to him` IS FALSE, `the amount allowed as a deduction under section 47(b)(1)` IS 5_000) EQUALS 180_000
#ASSERT `s 345(b)(1) — the annual income of another insured person` (`An insured person's assessed income for section 345` WITH `the income in the final assessment, before any exemption, deduction or credit` IS 200_000, `the contributions and equivalent tax allowed as a deduction under section 47A` IS 15_000, `the small-business deduction of section 87B applies to him` IS TRUE, `the amount allowed as a deduction under section 47(b)(1)` IS 5_000) EQUALS 195_000
-- (c)(1): due 30,000, advances 25,000, benefit difference 1,000: 4,000; difference 6,000 swallows it: 0; advances equal or more: 0.
#ASSERT `s 345(c)(1) — the difference the insured pays: contributions due` 30_000 `, advances paid` 25_000 `, benefit difference due to him` 1_000 EQUALS 4_000
#ASSERT `s 345(c)(1) — the difference the insured pays: contributions due` 30_000 `, advances paid` 25_000 `, benefit difference due to him` 6_000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 345(c)(1) — the difference the insured pays: contributions due` 30_000 `, advances paid` 25_000 `, benefit difference due to him` 0 EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `s 345(c)(1) — the difference the insured pays: contributions due` 30_000 `, advances paid` 30_000 `, benefit difference due to him` 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 345(c)(1) — the difference the insured pays: contributions due` 30_000 `, advances paid` 35_000 `, benefit difference due to him` 0 EQUALS 0
-- (e): the higher of the Schedule K minimum (3,442, the Institute's 2026 figure) and the last income updated.
#ASSERT `s 345(e) — the income on which the advance is paid: Schedule K minimum` 3_442 `, last income updated` 5_000 EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `s 345(e) — the income on which the advance is paid: Schedule K minimum` 3_442 `, last income updated` 3_000 EQUALS 3_442
#ASSERT `s 345(e) — the income on which the advance is paid: Schedule K minimum` 3_442 `, last income updated` 3_442 EQUALS 3_442

§§ `Section 345A: an allotment of shares`

#ASSERT `s 345A(b) — the first day of the month in which the income counts, for the charge date` (YMD 2026 5 20) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 1
#ASSERT `s 345A(b) — the employer for section 342(a), the employer at the allotment being` "A Ltd" `and on the charge date` "B Ltd" EQUALS "A Ltd"
#ASSERT `s 345A(c) — the monthly income with the allotment income: monthly income` 20_000 `plus` 5_000 EQUALS 25_000

§§ `Section 345B: an early pension`

`a pensioner of 10,000 with no other income` MEANS `A person receiving an early pension` WITH `the early pension paid to him in the month` IS 10_000, `his other income liable for contributions in the month` IS 0, `he has other income on which contributions are paid` IS FALSE
`a pensioner of 10,000 with other income of 45,000` MEANS `A person receiving an early pension` WITH `the early pension paid to him in the month` IS 10_000, `his other income liable for contributions in the month` IS 45_000, `he has other income on which contributions are paid` IS TRUE
`a pensioner of 10,000 with other income of 52,000` MEANS `A person receiving an early pension` WITH `the early pension paid to him in the month` IS 10_000, `his other income liable for contributions in the month` IS 52_000, `he has other income on which contributions are paid` IS TRUE
`a pensioner of 2,000 with no other income` MEANS `A person receiving an early pension` WITH `the early pension paid to him in the month` IS 2_000, `his other income liable for contributions in the month` IS 0, `he has other income on which contributions are paid` IS FALSE
`a pensioner of 2,000 with other income of 10,000` MEANS `A person receiving an early pension` WITH `the early pension paid to him in the month` IS 2_000, `his other income liable for contributions in the month` IS 10_000, `he has other income on which contributions are paid` IS TRUE
`a pensioner of 3,442 with no other income` MEANS `A person receiving an early pension` WITH `the early pension paid to him in the month` IS 3_442, `his other income liable for contributions in the month` IS 0, `he has other income on which contributions are paid` IS FALSE
`a pensioner of 60,000 with no other income` MEANS `A person receiving an early pension` WITH `the early pension paid to him in the month` IS 60_000, `his other income liable for contributions in the month` IS 0, `he has other income on which contributions are paid` IS FALSE

-- Maximum 51,910 and minimum 3,442 (the Institute's printed 2026 figures that row IL-05 carries).
-- 10,000 with no other income: within the maximum: 10,000. With other income 45,000: the room is 51,910 - 45,000 = 6,910. With 52,000: no room: 0.
-- 2,000 with no other income: raised to the minimum 3,442. With other income: not raised, and within the room (41,910): 2,000. Exactly the minimum: 3,442. 60,000: capped at 51,910.
#ASSERT `s 345B(c) — the early pension on which contributions are paid: the person` `a pensioner of 10,000 with no other income` `, maximum income` 51_910 `, minimum income` 3_442 EQUALS 10_000
#ASSERT `s 345B(c) — the early pension on which contributions are paid: the person` `a pensioner of 10,000 with other income of 45,000` `, maximum income` 51_910 `, minimum income` 3_442 EQUALS 6_910
#ASSERT `s 345B(c) — the early pension on which contributions are paid: the person` `a pensioner of 10,000 with other income of 52,000` `, maximum income` 51_910 `, minimum income` 3_442 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 345B(c) — the early pension on which contributions are paid: the person` `a pensioner of 2,000 with no other income` `, maximum income` 51_910 `, minimum income` 3_442 EQUALS 3_442
#ASSERT `s 345B(c) — the early pension on which contributions are paid: the person` `a pensioner of 2,000 with other income of 10,000` `, maximum income` 51_910 `, minimum income` 3_442 EQUALS 2_000
#ASSERT `s 345B(c) — the early pension on which contributions are paid: the person` `a pensioner of 3,442 with no other income` `, maximum income` 51_910 `, minimum income` 3_442 EQUALS 3_442
#ASSERT `s 345B(c) — the early pension on which contributions are paid: the person` `a pensioner of 60,000 with no other income` `, maximum income` 51_910 `, minimum income` 3_442 EQUALS 51_910

-- (e)(2), threshold 7,703: other income 5,000: room 2,703: pension 10,000 -> 2,703; pension 1,000 -> 1,000; other income at or over the threshold: 0; none: 7,703.
#ASSERT `s 345B(e)(2) — the part of the early pension of one who also works that is charged at the reduced rate: pension` 10_000 `, other income` 5_000 `, threshold` 7_703 EQUALS 2_703
#ASSERT `s 345B(e)(2) — the part of the early pension of one who also works that is charged at the reduced rate: pension` 1_000 `, other income` 5_000 `, threshold` 7_703 EQUALS 1_000
#ASSERT `s 345B(e)(2) — the part of the early pension of one who also works that is charged at the reduced rate: pension` 10_000 `, other income` 7_703 `, threshold` 7_703 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 345B(e)(2) — the part of the early pension of one who also works that is charged at the reduced rate: pension` 10_000 `, other income` 8_000 `, threshold` 7_703 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 345B(e)(2) — the part of the early pension of one who also works that is charged at the reduced rate: pension` 10_000 `, other income` 0 `, threshold` 7_703 EQUALS 7_703

§§ `Sections 346 and 347`

#ASSERT `s 346 — the annual income of one the Institute insured at his request, the regulations fixing` (JUST 1_234) EQUALS 1_234
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 346 — the annual income of one the Institute insured at his request, the regulations fixing` NOTHING BECAUSE "the regulations fixing the income of one the Institute insured at his request are not deposited"
#ASSERT     `s 347 — the clerk may determine the contributions: from` `an employee` `to` `a self-employed person` `, the clerk being appointed` TRUE
#ASSERT     `s 347 — the clerk may determine the contributions: from` `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed` `to` `an employee` `, the clerk being appointed` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 347 — the clerk may determine the contributions: from` `an employee` `to` `an employee` `, the clerk being appointed` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 347 — the clerk may determine the contributions: from` `an employee` `to` `a self-employed person` `, the clerk being appointed` FALSE
